title: Match-3 boards
intro: Swap gems to line up three of a kind: they clear, the gems above fall into the gaps, new ones drop in, and whatever lands in a line clears too. No code.
project: Empty | Gem Swap

chapter: A board of gems | Entity, Create Match Board
create: Match Board
explain: menu:Entity | Entity, Create Match Board | Create Match Board makes an eight by eight board, dealt already so you can see it.
explain: component:Tilemap | The gems are tiles | The gems are the tiles of a tilemap, so a board is painted like any level. With no tileset each kind of gem is a square of its own color.
explain: field:MatchBoard.Gems | Gems | These tile numbers are gems, six kinds. Any other tile on the board is a block the gems stop on.
explain: field:MatchBoard.Deal | Deal and Seed | Each game deals a fresh board with nothing lined up and a move to make. A seed makes it the same board every time, which is handy for a puzzle, and for this demo.
set: MatchBoard.Seed = 152
explain: group:MatchBoard.Rules | Rules | Only swaps that line something up are allowed, gaps refill from the top, and a board with no move left is shuffled.
explain: field:MatchBoard.MatchMessage | Match Message | As gems clear the board sends Match, with how many cleared.
deselect
create: Text
rename: Gems Cleared
add: ScreenAnchor
set: ScreenAnchor.Anchor = Top
set: ScreenAnchor.Offset = 0, -0.5
add: Counter
set: Counter.Message = Match
set: Counter.Format = Gems: {0}
explain: component:Counter | A counter | So a counter listening for Match adds up the gems cleared, a score with no code.

chapter: Swap, clear, fall | Click a gem, then its neighbor
play
wait: 0.5
say: Click a gem, then the one beside it, and they swap.
gameclick: -0.5, 2.5
wait: 0.3
gameclick: 0.5, 2.5
wait: 2
expectvalue: Board.MatchBoard.Swaps = 1
expectvalue: Gems Cleared.Text.Value = Gems: 6
explain: game | A chain | Three in a row cleared, the gems above fell into the gap, and the ones that landed lined up again and cleared too: a chain, six gems in all.
say: A swap that lines nothing up isn't allowed.
gameclick: -3.5, 3.5
wait: 0.3
gameclick: -2.5, 3.5
wait: 1
expectvalue: Board.MatchBoard.Swaps = 1
expecttile: Board 0, 0 = 3
explain: game | Back again | The two gems nudge into each other and slide straight back.

chapter: Keys and gamepads | A cursor, Space to pick a gem up, an arrow to swap
say: With keys or a gamepad, the arrows bring up a cursor in the middle of the board and move it.
tap: Right
wait: 0.3
tap: Right
wait: 0.3
tap: Right
wait: 0.3
tap: Up
wait: 0.4
say: Space picks the gem up, and an arrow swaps it that way.
tap: Space
wait: 0.4
tap: Down
wait: 2
expectvalue: Board.MatchBoard.Swaps = 2
expectvalue: Gems Cleared.Text.Value = Gems: 15
explain: game | Lined up | That lined up another match, and in it falls. The counter is up to fifteen gems.
stop
say: That's a match-3 board with no code. Its tiles are saved with the scene, so rewinding goes back to how the board was, and in a network game every player can swap.
